      "side": 1,
      "message": "The 50/200 is 50 for the gain of the INA213 and 1/200 is the gain of the sense resistor (i.e. 0.005).\n\nFor example when drawing 1amp from the power source:\nV,rsense     \u003d 0.005 * 1\nV,ina_output \u003d 50 * 0.005 (or 50/200) \u003d 0.25v\nV,ec         \u003d (20/(20+8.66)) * 0.25  \u003d 0.17446v\n\nTo scale the result to 1amp then V,ec * 1/((20/(20+8.66))*50/200) or V,ec * 143/25",
